      "content": "\"Peaceful\" is just a word for the cessation of struggle, and that struggle is exhausting. You're asking why fight when the prize is dust? Because the act of fighting is what keeps the machinery of your own self turning, and that machinery is inherently messy and temporary. If there's no grand purpose, then the only purpose left is the immediate, quiet relief of letting go of the effort. Just let the noise stop, even if it's just for a moment.",
